    body: "Missing a bill due date can cost you. Late fees on credit cards run $25 to $40. A missed phone bill can shut off your service. A late insurance payment can cancel your coverage. The good news is your iPhone already has a free tool that can remind you days ahead of time, with a sound and a banner on your screen. The Reminders app comes pre-installed on every iPhone. The white icon with three dotted lines sits on your home screen. It costs nothing, needs no signup, and works without an internet connection. Once you set a reminder, your phone will alert you on the day and time you pick, even if the phone is in your pocket. You can also set the reminder to repeat every month. So you only have to set it once for a recurring bill. This guide is written for someone using an iPhone for the first time. But it works for any iPhone running iOS 17 or newer (most iPhones from 2018 onward). We walk through opening the Reminders app, creating a new list called \"Bills,\" adding each bill with the right due date, setting a notification a few days before so you have time to act, and turning on monthly repeat. We also cover how to mark a bill as paid, how to delete an old reminder, and how to get reminders to show up on your Apple Watch or iPad if you have one. By the end, you will never miss a due date again. And you will not need to install any new apps. If you have trouble seeing small text, we share where to make the text bigger before you start. If you do not hear well, we cover how to make the alert sound louder or pick a stronger ringtone.",
